Done. Here's what changed:

**`src/lib.rs`** — Added `filter_by_tag`:

```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes.iter().filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag)).collect()
}
```

- Exact match on each tag in `note.tags` (via `any()` + `==`).
- Preserves input order (single pass, no sorting).
- Returns `Vec<&'a Note>` — no allocations of Note structs, just references.

**`src/main.rs`** — `list` command now accepts `--tag <TAG>`:

- Manual arg parsing (no external deps) scans args 2..N for `--tag <value>`.
- When present, calls `filter_by_tag(&notes, tag)` before printing.
- Without `--tag`, behaves identically to before (prints all notes).

